    The implementation of this 1 + 𝑛 rescue scheme, through hierarchical organization and task allocation
optimization, not only improves the response speed and efficiency of rescue operations but also strengthens
the adaptability to rescue needs under different maritime conditions and situations. Ultimately, this strategy
ensures more efficient and precise search and rescue actions, providing quicker and more effective rescue
services for those trapped in maritime emergencies.




                                                                                   型
IV. Search Model
    Search – Grid Probability Search Technique
    When the submersible went lost, the following search strategy is established to minimize the search




                                                                   模
time:

    • Acquire the possible location using the Predictive Location Model




                                                                  学
    • Properly rasterize the search region




                                                          数
    • Identify the Centre Search Grid and assign a probability to each grid

    • Update the Centre Search Grid by time till the objective searched

V. Extrapolation for Other Destinations   ：

                                                                      els
   Extrapolate - Expand the model to account for other tourist destinations.
                                         号

                                                                    od
   1. Adaptation for Other Destinations:
      The model can be used in various incident areas, incorporating regional variations in sea conditions
                                 众

      and topography. We try to transfer the model to the Caribbean Sea in this context. The ocean
                                                                   m
      currents in the Caribbean Sea predominantly move from east to west, aligning with our simulation
                         公


      results, which indicates the model’s applicability to other sea areas and its capability to predict the
                                                      H
      movement trends of submersibles.
                                                   AT
         信




   2. Multiple Submersibles:
      The model will update by overlaying each grid probability when the simultaneous loss of multiple s
      is considered. Therefore, only small changes need to be made to our model to copy with multiple
        微

                                             M


      submersible scenarios.

